// A LEVEL'S CONSTRUCTOR THAT IS NOT BUILT, refused before anything runs
// (SATELLITE_INFINITY.md). check.sh asserts both.
//
// REBASED AT INF-2 (2026-09-19). At INF-1 this displayed `satellite.infinity()`,
// which was a numbered word with no library; INF-2 built it, and it prints
// (infinity) now. The vehicle is the lettered level from INF-6's done-when,
// `satellite.aasat()`: no word has that spelling yet, so `satellite.` is read as the
// word and `aasat(` as a capsule this program never wrote.
//
// Red on purpose when INF-6 builds the family words; rebase it then onto whatever
// constructor is still unbuilt, never delete it.
satellite.include(satellite)

satellite.capsule satellite.main()
{
    satellite.console.display("before")
    satellite.console.display(satellite.aasat())
}

satellite.return(satellite)
